diff --git a/docs/LEVELS.md b/docs/LEVELS.md
index b2938f79..743919df 100644
--- a/docs/LEVELS.md
+++ b/docs/LEVELS.md
@@ -492,3 +492,80 @@ sample. No level uses a bank yet.
   banks (they need the same pack format with sprites), the 6 songs and the SFX (47,793 of 49,152 B used:
   an owner decision), and the GBA and PS1 readers of the texture bank.
 
+
+## LV7b: the audio kit (6 songs, 12 sound effects; plan 8.6, 9)
+
+Songs and effects for the new levels. Nothing plays them yet: the level packages point their maps at them,
+and the jukebox rows are not granted by anything yet.
+
+**How audio is built and loaded (read first).**
+- A song is four MML strings (`core/src/mml_<name>.c`, rows in `songs.c`). `tools/mmlc.py` compiles them into
+  cues of the music bank (`core/gen/mus_data.c`); the game plays the bank, not the strings (the old interpreter
+  in `audio_seq.c` is a test reference, dropped by the console links). The bank is `const` data: GBA ROM, PS1
+  EXE (resident), Dreamcast.
+- The SFX PCM (`tools/sfxgen.py` -> `core/gen/sfx_data.c`) is `const` in the GBA ROM; on the PS1 it is
+  `SFX.BIN` on the disc, uploaded to SPU RAM 0x2000-0x2FFFF (Talk is 0x30000-0x7DFFF).
+- The comedy-kit effects are not PCM: short segment tables in `audio_fx.c`, played on tone channels 2 and 3 by
+  `audio_tick()`. They cost 0 B of PCM and a few tens of bytes of ROM each.
+
+**The PCM budget decision.** `sfxgen.py --check` says 47,793 of 49,152 B (`AUDIO_SFX_BUDGET`): 1,359 B free,
+and twelve PCM effects need 20 to 25 KB. Default chosen by Claude (LEVELS), owner may override: the 12 new
+effects are synth one-shots (appended after `SFX_CREAK`), so the PCM budget, `SFX.BIN` and the PS1 SPU map do
+not move at all. `sfxgen.py --synth` audits them (see the table).
+
+**The six songs** (`SONG_SPA_BOSSA` .. `SONG_GREAT_RAIN`, ids 29..34 after `SONG_NUMBER_TEN`;
+`SONG_OLD_COUNT` 29, `SONG_COUNT_ALL` 35). 8 bars on every channel, one tempo, loop from bar 1:
+
+| song | id | name in the jukebox | bpm | pass | for |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `SONG_SPA_BOSSA` | 29 | Spa Day, Sort Of | 120 | 16.0 s | the spa: a bossa nova, a little too relaxed (Dm7 G7 Cmaj7 Am7 D7) |
+| `SONG_BANDSTAND` | 30 | Bandstand Incident | 132 | 14.6 s | oompah gone wrong: the lead is a semitone off for two bars, the tuba ends on the wrong note |
+| `SONG_FILING` | 31 | Filing Cabinet March | 104 | 18.5 s | a filing-office march: snare, bell lead, chords on the off beat |
+| `SONG_LEDGER` | 32 | The Ledger March | 92 | 20.9 s | a ledger march in A minor, the adding machine on the drums |
+| `SONG_ARREARS` | 33 | Duchess of Arrears | 96 | 15.0 s | the Duchess's theme: a stately minuet in D minor, 3/4 |
+| `SONG_GREAT_RAIN` | 34 | The Great Rain | 72 | 26.7 s | New Game+: E minor, a music box over a slow pad, rain on the noise channel |
+
+The dark levels reuse the quiet old songs (Wall Lullaby, Hell Lullaby, Thirteen Bells, Sad, Ominous, the
+Mingle music box); no new dark song was written.
+
+- **Ids.** Jukebox unlocks 726..731 (`UL_STORY_SONG3(s)`, `unlocks_story.c`, listed under the Songs shelf in
+  story mode only after a grant; free play lists all). Nothing grants them yet. 732..735 stay spare. Bank cue
+  ids: 228..231 (`classic.lock`; 232.. is the sfx area) and 198, 199 (`common.lock`), through `mus_bind.c`.
+- **Checks.** Each song is rendered with the real sequencer and a small host synth (not committed; the WAVs
+  are in the package's evidence folder): no clipping (peak 0.27..0.41 of 1.00), and the same number of notes
+  every pass (a clean loop). `core/tests/test_levels_audio.c`: ids appended and unchanged, songs valid and
+  loop inside 6..32 s, every channel under 300 B, bank cues present and unique, jukebox rows present, none
+  unlocked in a new story game. `test_music_hash.c` has a golden row per new song (the old rows are untouched).
+
+**The twelve effects** (`SFX_VALVE` .. `SFX_RAIN`, after `SFX_CREAK`; `SFX_SYNTH_OLD_END` 15 old +
+12). Each is at most 12 frames (0.4 s). Audit (`python3 tools/sfxgen.py --synth`; peak of a 8 kHz rendering,
+share of full scale):
+
+| effect | tables | frames | peak | what it is |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `SFX_VALVE` | 21 B | 10 | 51 % | steam hiss and a metal thunk |
+| `SFX_TUBE` | 20 B | 10 | 33 % | the pneumatic tube: a rising rush, then a pop |
+| `SFX_STAMP` | 21 B | 3 | 59 % | rubber stamp on a form |
+| `SFX_SHOWTIME` | 42 B | 12 | 49 % | the showtime stinger: three notes, a held one, a cymbal |
+| `SFX_ZIPLINE` | 23 B | 12 | 29 % | a whirr that climbs |
+| `SFX_RAFT` | 20 B | 12 | 19 % | wood creak, then a splash |
+| `SFX_TOWHOOK` | 36 B | 6 | 53 % | three clanks down a chain |
+| `SFX_TILL` | 26 B | 12 | 53 % | ka-CHING |
+| `SFX_GAVEL` | 33 B | 8 | 65 % | two knocks |
+| `SFX_SCREAM` | 28 B | 12 | 36 % | a cartoon scream that climbs (comic, no gore) |
+| `SFX_PAGE` | 20 B | 8 | 16 % | a page turn |
+| `SFX_RAIN` | 32 B | 12 | 23 % | soft patter and three drops (loop it by calling it again) |
+
+PCM before and after: 47,793 B, unchanged (`sfxgen.py --check`; the 36 old PCM ids and the 15 old synth ids
+keep their numbers). Table bytes: about 0.34 KB of GBA ROM in all.
+
+**Per platform.**
+- GBA: the six cues (1,512 B with their directory rows) and the 12 recipes are ROM only. No RAM.
+- Dreamcast: the same core data, nothing platform-specific.
